From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:08:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mouse: Show the touchpad page under Caminito

The page was shown when XInput listed a touchpad. Under Caminito the
capplet runs on XWayland, whose devices are virtual pointers with no
libinput or Synaptics properties, so a laptop's touchpad was never
found there. Where MATE_WM_NAME says Caminito the page is always shown:
Caminito applies the org.mate.peripherals-touchpad keys to the touchpads
it has, and to none on a machine without one.

On X11, and under any other Wayland compositor, the page is shown as it
was.
---
 capplets/mouse/msd-input-helper.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/capplets/mouse/msd-input-helper.c b/capplets/mouse/msd-input-helper.c
index 7dc0d996..e03d44a9 100644
--- a/capplets/mouse/msd-input-helper.c
+++ b/capplets/mouse/msd-input-helper.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <X11/Xatom.h>
 
 #include "msd-input-helper.h"
+#include "wm-common.h"
 
 gboolean
 supports_xinput_devices (void)
@@ -100,6 +101,12 @@ touchpad_is_present (void)
         guint i;
         gboolean retval;
 
+        /* Under Caminito the capplet runs on XWayland, whose input devices
+         * are virtual and say nothing of the machine's. Caminito applies
+         * the touchpad keys to the touchpads it has itself. */
+        if (wm_common_is_caminito ())
+                return TRUE;
+
         if (supports_xinput_devices () == FALSE)
                 return TRUE;
 
